{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "002Z", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{remark-preorder-versus-partial-order}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\noindent\n", "suffix": "\n\n"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ddeafe914cec111f72d89e5385fa099f39ae48a2e761687e72c0414e00a5231a", "source_text": "The upshot of Remark <REF_0001>\nis that while computing a colimit of a system or a limit of\nan inverse system, we may always assume the preorder is a partial order.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4841e4344192447be845f37c35709df44f084bcba8903c789a6378717000ef3f", "unit_id": "tag:002Z:p005"}
